s, restaurants and opportunities for specialty shopping, and the inner city is dotted with art installations.","grounding":[{"source":"wikivoyage","title":"Horsens","url":"https://en.wikivoyage.org/wiki/Horsens","licence":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}],"short":"Horsens is a port city of sixty thousand in eastern Jutland, Denmark. Boller Slot and the grounds at Bygholm carry most of the nine hours of sights, and CASA Arena Horsens is the other landmark. June to August, with the lake at Mosso close by.","short_src":"rewrite","facts":{"population":61074,"visit_h":7.2}},"highlights":[{"id":"hl-casa-arena-horsens","name":"CASA Arena Horsens","kind":"Landmark","lat":55.8716,"lon":9.8576,"dist_km":1.3,"rank_score":7.1,"resolved_by":"catalogue","image":{"url":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/c/cd/Ac_horsens.jpg/960px-Ac_horsens.jpg","author":"Pathfinder77","licence":"CC BY-SA 3.0","licence_url":"https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/3.0","page":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Ac_horsens.jpg","w":1632,"h":1224,"ok_print":true}}],"do":[{"name":"Mossø","type":"swim","detail":"20 km away, water rated Excellent","ref":{"layer":"lakes","cc":"DK","id":"dk-moss-Q3435105"},"sources":["eea","layer"],"evidence":{"method":"open","n_sources":2,"sources":["eea","layer"]}},{"name":"Canoeing at Bygholm Sø","type":"activity","sources":["wikivoyage"],"evidence":{"method":"open","n_sources":1,"sources":["wikivoyage"],"curated":"wikivoyage_do"}},{"name":"European Medieval Festival","type":"activity","sources":["wikivoyage"],"evidence":{"method":"open","n_sources":1,"sources":["wikivoyage"],"curated":"wikivoyage_do"}},{"name":"Fængslet","type":"activity","sources":["wikivoyage"],"evidence":{"method":"open","n_sources":1,"sources":["wikivoyage"],"curated":"wikivoyage_do"}},{"name":"Horsens Ny Teater","type":"activity","sources":["wikivoyage"],"evidence":{"method":"open","n_sources":1,"sources":["wikivoyage"],"curated":"wikivoyage_do"}}],"nearby":{"lakes":[{"layer":"lakes","c